---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/data/site";
const updated = "2026-08-31";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How TinyTools handles data: calculator inputs stay in your browser, analytics and advertising cookies require your consent, and you can change your choice at any time."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy Policy" }]} />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>31 August 2026</time></p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ("we", "us") collects when
      you use <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>, why, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The numbers you type into a calculator are processed entirely in your browser. We never receive or store them.</li>
      <li>We use Google Analytics to understand which pages and tools are useful. Analytics and advertising cookies are only set after you accept them.</li>
      <li>We intend to show ads from Google AdSense. When ads are live, they are only served after you consent, and consent controls whether they are personalised.</li>
      <li>You can accept or reject non-essential cookies when you first visit, and change your choice any time via "Cookie settings" in the footer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Calculator inputs</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculation runs locally in your browser using client-side
      JavaScript. Hours, pay rates, salaries, and tax settings are not
      transmitted to us or to any third party, and are not stored on a server.
      Some tools put your inputs in the page URL so you can bookmark or share a
      result; that URL is only created if you choose to copy or share it.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID <code>{SITE.ga4Id}</code>). With
      your consent it sets cookies and collects: pages viewed, referring site,
      approximate location (country/region, derived from IP — the full IP address
      is not stored by us), device and browser type, and interaction events such
      as "a calculation was completed" or "a result was copied". We use this only
      in aggregate to decide which calculators to improve or build next. If you
      do not consent, Google Analytics runs in a cookieless mode that does not
      identify you or store data on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} plans to display ads served by Google AdSense (publisher ID
      <code>{SITE.adsensePublisherId}</code>). No ad units are shown on the site
      yet and the AdSense script is not currently loaded — only a meta tag and
      an <code>ads.txt</code> entry declare the publisher account. When ads are
      switched on they will load only after you accept advertising cookies, and
      before that point Consent Mode keeps advertising storage denied by default.
      When ads are active and you have consented, Google and its partners may use
      cookies to serve and measure ads, including personalised ads. If you reject
      advertising cookies, any ads shown are non-personalised or suppressed
      depending on your region. You can review Google's practices at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar storage</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consent choice</strong> — stored in your browser's local storage so we don't ask again on every visit. Essential; not shareable.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — set only with your consent; used to distinguish sessions and users for aggregate reporting.</li>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — set only with your consent, and only when ads are active; used for ad serving, frequency capping, and measurement.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process your IP address and
      request metadata in server logs to deliver the site and protect against
      abuse, as described in the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="nofollow">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live (including the EEA, the UK, and California) you
      may have the right to access, correct, or delete personal data, to object
      to or restrict processing, and to withdraw consent. Because we do not hold
      an account or profile for you, the main control available on this site is
      your cookie consent choice, which you can change at any time. For requests
      about data held by Google, use Google's own tools. To contact us, see the
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a general-audience tools site and is not directed to children
      under 13 (or the equivalent age in your country). We do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this page if our data practices change and will revise the
      "last updated" date above.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
